    "source": "Bad Eden Bulwark + Shadow Courier v1.0 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Movement is now a doctrine of the body.</em></p><p>While you hold <strong>at least 1 Surge</strong>: you are immune to forced movement, the Staggered condition, and any effect that would stun, paralyze or render you unconscious without first reducing your Integrity to 0.</p><p>At the start of your turn you may spend any number of Surge: <strong>+1 square</strong> of movement for each, for that turn only. You may pass through the space of any creature or unattended object softer than reinforced stone (GM call) without stopping, and you do not provoke reaction strikes while doing so.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
